From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 20:15:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08502/11362] Extend Simplified Technical English rule to all
 project prose, not just CLAUDE.md

Operator follow-up directive: "We want that to apply to all prose written,
not just when writing to Claude.md." Append-only scope extension per this
file's own never-prune convention -- the original CLAUDE.md-only rule text
from the prior commit stays verbatim; a new SCOPE EXTENSION section broadens
coverage to ops/*.md, docs/*.md, openspec specs, epics stories, code
comments/docstrings (aligned with the existing comment-calibration rule,
not duplicating it), commit messages, agent task prompts, and the
assistant's own written responses while working on this project.

Still forward-only, still STE100-spirit (not the formal dictionary), still
honor-discipline (no lint) -- none of the three prior scope/strictness/
enforcement choices changed, only the surface area. Explicitly does not
override the Public Documentation Discipline's content rules or the
operator-curated-doc protections -- this is a sentence-style rule, not a
who-may-edit or what-content-is-allowed rule.

Header and Rule Index entry updated with a SCOPE EXTENDED status marker,
matching the file's existing RETIRED/SUPERSEDED banner convention, so the
broadened scope is discoverable without rewriting the original rule prose.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
